{
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "description": "Values outside the grammar of the spec's `.regexp` patterns, for protocol version 1. The control matches the whole string, so a conformant decoder refuses every vector here, at decoding or at validation: a capability verb with two colons, a trailing space or newline or a leading hyphen, a domain with trailing text, a trailing newline or an embedded separator, and the three verb fields of token claims. Each vector is well-formed CBOR in the shape of a valid frame (kind frame) or token-claims map (kind token-claims) with one such value, carries refused: true and the CDDL rule it breaks, and carries valid_control_wire_hex, the same bytes with a value inside the grammar, which every consumer must accept so that a vector cannot be refused for another reason. message and wire_hex follow the shared round-trip contract. The room-path and device-id-hex patterns occur only in the room-notice claims, which the implementations' own schema and parser tests pin.",
